# Narrow witnesses preserved with the theorem

All are analytic source/review witnesses, not new scientific executions or an exhaustive no-go survey.

| Substitution | Witness and consequence |
| --- | --- |
| Forward-only dirty route | Labels(a,b,c) become(b,c,a); the required final reverse swap gives(c,b,a) and restores the intermediate record. |
| Reassert unused purity after disturbance | A flip of an unused vacuum block makes its next exchange put a1 into S. Either prove ideal endpoint identity or charge the disturbance. |
| Count an uncompensated wait only as H0 aging | H0=0,K_Z=I+X,ready\|0> gives trace error2\|sin g\| during an omitted waitg, with no implementation fault relative to nominalK_Z. Price the actual segment or comparison residual. |
| Treat B_C as exact action | Any strict B_C>\|C\| gives a strict allowance; exact compensation action is\|C\|sum A_u. |
| Normalize the good branch | Conditioning can change the old/reference/F marginal; use vacuum tensor the exact unconditioned complement and g(delta). |
| Retarget to faulty midpoint for free | Changing the state and its complementary marginal needs an additional allowance; the published target remains the modeled compression marginal. |
| Infer restoration from dirty transit | Returned routes preserve occupied records; they do not convert consumed record blocks back into supplied pure inputs or the raw source law. |

These witnesses protect specified proof steps and hypotheses. They neither count five fictional alternatives nor claim all memory mechanisms impossible. Full source/review bodies preserve the detailed derivations and their scope.
